  "body": "### Summary\n\nAs a poster, I want characters that HFR would cut (emoji outside the BMP) silently blocked while I type, as in the legacy app, so that I never lose the end of a message.\n\n### Scope\n\nUXD-16, option A (operator decision 2026-11-02 on [#379](https://github.com/ezzz/HFRnow/issues/379)): the legacy composer silently blocks keyboard emoji while typing. The shipped LOT-084 lets them be typed and refuses at send (`docs/lots/LOT-084-reply-composer.md`, step 4). Block them while typing; keep the send-time refusal as the safety net for pasted text. The refusal with a smiley suggestion (LOT-151) is an evolution and moves to M5.\n\n- Milestone: **M2** (the UXD-16 row says \"A in M2\"). A small (a) item, a port of the legacy behaviour. Follow-up of LOT-084 (#176). Tracked by [#413](https://github.com/ezzz/HFRnow/issues/413).\n- Module: App · Difficulty: easy · Priority: medium.\n- Legacy sources (read-only, `origin/master` @ 2440d79): GAP-095 in `docs/migration/GAP-LEGACY-VS-SWIFT.md` cites the file and symbol.\n\n### Depends on\n\n- LOT-084 (#176, done)\n\n### Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] Typing a non-BMP character from the keyboard inserts nothing and shows nothing (legacy); pasted text still reaches the send-time refusal.\n- [ ] View logic lives in `@Observable @MainActor` models tested with Swift Testing in `App/SwiftHFRTests/`; each new test is shown to fail without the change.\n- [ ] `xcodebuild build test` green on the iPhone 18 Pro and an iPad simulator (iOS 27.0), and the `App build + tests` CI job green.\n- [ ] UI strings in French; no new dependency; no HFR fact without a source.\n\n### Before you start (agents and humans)\n\nRead, in order: AGENTS.md, CLAUDE.md, docs/agents/ORCHESTRATION.md, docs/agents/REVIEW-ROUNDS.md, docs/agents/LESSONS.md, CONTRIBUTING.md, App/README.md and the LOT-084 spec. Claim with `/claim <session-id>` on this issue before writing code; PR body `Closes #<this issue>` + `Claim: <session-id>`; the app code starts with the `// Port of … @ 2440d79` comment (AGENTS.md §4).\n\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
